"""HM-19 - Bluetooth Low Energy 5.0 module with a UART, TI CC2640R2F inside. Bare module.

Datasheet: JNHuaMao "HM Bluetooth module datasheet", Last Version V107 (2019-02): section 1
(parameters, p3), section 3 (module table, p5), 6.5 (HM-19 schematic, p10), 6.6 (size, p10), 6.8
(device terminal functions, p11-12), 7 (system KEY and LED functions, p13). The silicon is the TI
CC2640R2F (datasheet SWRS204C).

Pins (V107 6.8): 1 UART_RTS (DIO_9), 2 UART_TX (DIO_2), 3 UART_CTS (DIO_0), 4 UART_RX (DIO_1),
5-6 NC (CC2640 debug), 7 NC (DIO_3), 8 KEY "System KEY" (DIO_4), 9 VCC, 10 "NC or VCC", 11 RESETB
"Reset if low >1000ms", 12 GND, 13 PIO3 (DIO_5), 14 PIO2 (DIO_6), 15 PIO1 "System LED" (DIO_7),
16 PIO0 "input/output pin" (DIO_8). Pin 10 joins VCC here, as in the vendor schematic (6.5).

Supply: section 3 gives the HM-19 VDD as 2.1-3.7 V; section 1 says "+1.9~3.7 VDC 50mA". The
narrower range is the declared one. Current: 50 mA (section 1), 2.6 mA in standby and active
(section 1).

The datasheet is inconsistent on the key: the pin table names pin 8 KEY, while the vendor
schematic (6.5) and the AT command "Query/Set PIO0 function (System KEY)" put the key on PIO0
(pin 16). A key press held over 1000 ms disconnects a connected module, and in standby restores
the factory settings (section 7). RESETB: the CC2640R2F RESET_N has no internal pull-up
(SWRS204C pin description); the HM-19 datasheet does not say whether the module adds one, and the
vendor schematic leaves RESETB open.

Levels: CC2640R2F VIH 0.8 VDDS, VIL 0.2 VDDS (SWRS204C 8.25); outputs 4 mA at VOH >= 2.72 V
with VDDS = 3.0 V.

Integrator-owned circuitry (vendor schematic, 6.5): 1 kOhm in series with UART_TX and UART_RX,
10 uF and 100 nF on VCC, the status LED with its resistor on PIO1 (470 Ohm), the key on PIO0.
Mechanics (6.6): 13.5 x 18.5 x 2.3 mm (0.8 mm board); pad 1 sits 7 mm from the top edge, which
holds the antenna, and the footprint leaves that part of the body off the pads.
"""

load("@stdlib/interfaces.zen", "Uart")

# V107 section 3: HM-19 VDD 2.1-3.7 V (section 1: 1.9-3.7 V).
VCC = io(Power(voltage="2.1V to 3.7V"))
GND = io(Ground)
UART = io(Uart)
RTS = io(Net, optional=True)
CTS = io(Net, optional=True)
KEY = io(Net, optional=True)
RESETB = io(Net, optional=True)
PIO0 = io(Net, optional=True)
PIO1 = io(Net, optional=True)
PIO2 = io(Net, optional=True)
PIO3 = io(Net, optional=True)

Component(
    name="HM19",
    prefix="U",
    symbol=Symbol(library="HM-19.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("HM-19.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="HM-19", manufacturer="JNHuaMao"),
    pins={
        "VCC": VCC,
        "GND": GND,
        "UART_TX": UART.TX,
        "UART_RX": UART.RX,
        "UART_RTS": RTS,
        "UART_CTS": CTS,
        "KEY": KEY,
        "RESETB": RESETB,
        "PIO0": PIO0,
        "PIO1": PIO1,
        "PIO2": PIO2,
        "PIO3": PIO3,
    },
)
